Krita Nova 31 - open and save with the Wacom Explorer (Android)

When the user's file explorer (Wacom Explorer, package com.example.fileexplorer,
github.com/Novaillusion/Nova_file_exlorer) is installed, File > Open, Import,
Save As and Export use it instead of Android's system file picker.

KoFileDialog.cpp (Android): for OpenFile/ImportFile, OpenFiles/ImportFiles and
SaveFile (after the existing "Save As:" format choice), Krita sends the
explorer's own requests to its PickerActivity:
  com.example.fileexplorer.action.OPEN_DOCUMENT   (like ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT)
  com.example.fileexplorer.action.CREATE_DOCUMENT (like ACTION_CREATE_DOCUMENT)
with the MIME type, EXTRA_TITLE (suggested name, with the chosen extension),
EXTRA_ALLOW_MULTIPLE and com.example.fileexplorer.extra.EXTENSIONS (the file
extensions of the dialog's filters, so the explorer dims the rest), and waits
for the result (QtAndroid::startActivity). The explorer answers with document
URIs of its documents provider, readable and writable; Krita keeps access to
them (takePersistableUriPermission). They are content:// URIs like the system
picker's, so opening, saving, autosave and recent files work as before.

If the explorer is not installed, the request can't be started, or
[File Dialogs] UseNovaExplorer=false is set in kritarc, the system picker is
used as before. Folder pickers always use the system picker.

AndroidManifest.xml: <queries> for com.example.fileexplorer, without which
Android 11+ hides the explorer from Krita.
